**What RESP is (Redis protocol)**
Redis speaks a text protocol called RESP. When you send a command, you don’t just send `"GET foo"`. You send an **array** of bulk strings.

The general format is:

```
*<number of items>\r\n
$<len of item1>\r\n
<item1>\r\n
$<len of item2>\r\n
<item2>\r\n
...
```

So `GET key` looks like:

```
*2\r\n
$3\r\n
GET\r\n
$3\r\n
key\r\n
```

### What `*1`, `*2`, `*3` mean
They are the RESP **array length**:
- `*1` means “this command has 1 argument”
- `*2` means “this command has 2 arguments”
- `*3` means “this command has 3 arguments”

Examples:
- `PING` → `*1 ...` (just one word)
- `GET key` → `*2 ...` (command + key)
- `SET key value` → `*3 ...` (command + key + value)

---

## The helper functions you asked about

### `respBulk(s: str) -> str`
This makes a **bulk string**:

```ferret
